pwa/dist/

# Generated previews (track maps, gameplay screenshots) — tooling output,
# regenerated on demand with `make track` / `make screenshots`.
#
# ANCHORED to the root on purpose. Unanchored, this pattern matches a
# directory called `previews` at any depth — including
# pwa/public/previews/, which is not tooling output at all: those are the
# campaign menu's biome banners, and they SHIP with the site.
/previews/

# Recorded runs (`make record`, and the SAVE RUN DATA button) — a drive is
# somebody's own measurement, not repository content.
runs/

# Release scratch
.release-notes.md

# Store submission OUTPUT. The authored source is native/store/listing.mts and
# scripts/store-shots/recipes.mjs; everything below is regenerated by
# `make store-metadata` and `make store-shots`, and gitignored for the reason
# pwa/dist is (§11.2): reviewing a 2868x1320 PNG diff in a pull request helps
# nobody. The capsule art under tauri/store/capsules/ is NOT here — that is
# authored art, not build output.
# THE LISTING'S OWN WORDS. The game is PAID on the App Store and OPEN SOURCE
# here, and the marketing copy is the one thing those two pull apart: a
# description, subtitle, promo text and keyword set are what the store indexes
# and what a competitor reads, so publishing them puts the paid listing's own
# prose on a crawlable page under somebody else's domain. The RULES stay
# committed (native/store/listing.mts), a SKELETON documents the shape
# (copy.example.mts), and the `store-listing` skill carries the craft — the
# knowledge is in the repository and the words are not. Nothing backs this file
# up: keep a copy outside the checkout.
native/store/copy.mts

native/store/store.config.json
native/store/screenshots/
native/fastlane/metadata/
tauri/store/steam-listing.md
tauri/store/screenshots/

# The App Store Connect API key, and any Play service-account JSON. Credentials,
# and this repository is public. `native/.env` is already covered above.
native/*.p8
native/*-service-account.json
